# PAM for sudo in an egzo agent: egzo writes the agent's uid into /etc/passwd but not /etc/shadow, so pam_unix refuses the account
# ("account validation failure"). The agent is the only user of its sandbox and sudoers lets it in without a password, so PAM
# permits it; whether sudo can make it root at all is decided by no-new-privileges (drop_capabilities).
auth     sufficient pam_permit.so
account  sufficient pam_permit.so
session  sufficient pam_permit.so
